# L §3.3 accrue takes "yearly rate r": a monthly rate is refused; the period is in the value, found at run, so
# tally 2.1.7 (R5, issue #144; P66 reopened) prints RUN-DOMAIN at the value with load's words (L §8.4); 2.1.6
# printed LOAD-UNIT for the whole reality.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input p: money PLN
input r: rate
input d1: date
input d2: date
def a: num PLN = accrue(p, r, d1, d2, act365, simple) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  p = 1 000.00 PLN
  r = 1 %/month
  d1 = 2026-01-01
  d2 = 2026-07-01

ask q: a law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-DOMAIN accrue takes a yearly rate, not 0.01 /month (L §3.3)
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
